title: Replay on a copy rolled back to the moment, and check that the viewnode IDs match.
pid: fafbb4e7-6f3a-46d7-8a6f-b8559fd4833e
body: |2-
  Copy the data root and every skgrepo its config reaches (Jeff's reaches
  '../claude/...'), '.git' included, into the scratchpad, keeping their relative
  places and leaving out 'RETIRED', the run folders and '.index.tantivy'. There is
  no rsync: 'tar cf - --exclude=... jeff claude | (cd COPY && tar xf -)'. Give the
  copy's config another port, and start the server from inside the copy, recording
  its PID, as the 'verify' skill says. Then undo what happened after the moment:
  take out lines a later save added, delete nodes born later, and drop from
  'processed-marks-STEM.json' any mark set later.
  Open the view and compare it with what the user copied. Viewnode IDs are handed
  out in drawing order, so if the user's IDs (e.g. '4l') fall on the same headlines,
  the copy draws what the user's server drew. A note the user wrote about the bug
  can change the view by itself: a link in it changes its target's mentioners,
  which adds a root. To see collateral rerenders, run a skg-for-ai daemon on the
  copy's port; its log names what each save rerendered.
